"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Discovery evidence: a one-unit runtime spy observed four Popen calls in order: one Pandoc invocation and three git rev-parse --show-toplevel invocations on the cold path. Across all 884 production conversions, the same spy counted 1,770 Popen calls total, consistent with 884 Pandoc launches plus 886 repository-root discovery launches after warmup. This ticket intentionally remains open and unclaimed until the active independent-golden remediation lands.","timestamp":1786684090666221001}],"created_at":1786684024685021001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"285a3892-360b-4ec6-a04b-199732a7ec1c","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"cc7f-4a24-bc7a-4511"}],"description":"## Context\nA runtime Popen trace of the 884-unit wiki hardening oracle on origin/main 72731d3745 observed 1,770 process launches during the production conversion half. One cold conversion launched Pandoc once plus git rev-parse --show-toplevel three times; after warmup the loop averaged one extra git root-discovery subprocess per unit. The changeable seam is _convert calling _pandoc_timeout for every unit, which calls load_config and repeatedly rediscovers the repository root. This is independent of the duplicate legacy Pandoc oracle tracked by absolute-diplomatic-snowyowl.\n\n## Plan\n- Confirm exact warm and cold subprocess attribution and wall time under representative contention.\n- Compare maintained OSS practice for loop-invariant configuration lookup in hot paths and search prior rebar tickets for rejected caching or pass-level configuration injection.\n- Preserve timeout configurability and all timeout, fallback, and process-group reap behavioral coverage while moving repository/config discovery out of the per-unit loop.\n- Use held-out RED to GREEN and defect-seeded mutation before Gerrit submission.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] One render pass does not launch git root-discovery subprocesses once per Pandoc-bound unit.\n- [ ] Runtime timeout configuration remains observable at the documented render-pass boundary.\n- [ ] Timeout, fallback, and process-group reap contract tests retain equivalent behavioral coverage.\n- [ ] Before and after timing quantifies runner-seconds saved without reducing corpus or contractual coverage.\n- [ ] OSS comparison and prior-ticket disposition are recorded.\n- [ ] Gerrit LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 pass before merge.","env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["ci","performance","ubuntu","pandoc"],"ticket_id":"2364-663e-859d-4b58","ticket_type":"task","title":"Eliminate per-unit git root discovery from Pandoc conversion","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["c4dfc291-7887-457d-b3f5-8057c53bd73d","285a3892-360b-4ec6-a04b-199732a7ec1c","70441b51-51f0-410a-a9d3-390f52377aaf"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786688861395245275,"uuid":"ecb43122-c862-46a2-9470-3190a78d6ebb"}